      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so it's basically like giving the nervous system a chance to reset. i've had clients tell me it feels like they've just lost their \"drive\" or that their strength is being \"held back\" by something they can't see. from a physiological standpoint, what does that sudden stall actually look like in terms of the body's feedback loops?",
